      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s4"
      },
      "text": "In 2017, Tom Bennett and Barry Vengerik published Behind the CARBANAK Backdoor, which was the product of a deep and broad analysis of CARBANAK samples and FIN7 activity across several years.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "I added Russian language input to an analysis VM and used Microsoft’s on-screen keyboard (osk.exe) to navigate the Cyrillic keyboard layout and look up definitions.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_18",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 5,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p5_s1"
      },
      "text": "Figure 4 shows a Command and Control (C2) user interface for CARBANAK that I translated.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_20",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p8_s1"
      },
      "text": "Down the Rabbit Hole: When Having Source Code Does Not Help In simpler backdoors, a single function evaluates the command ID received from the C2 server and dispatches control to the correct function to carry out the command.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_27",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 9,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p9_s5"
      },
      "text": "CARBANAK’s named pipe-based tasking component is flexible enough to control both inherent command handlers and plugins.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 10,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p10_s1"
      },
      "text": "In fact, not only did we write such a client to aid in analysis and testing, but such a client, named botcmd.exe, was also present in the source dump.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_34",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 10,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p10_s7"
      },
      "text": "Even so, CARBANAK’s tasking component (for handling commands sent by the C2 server) serves as a counter-example.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_35",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 10,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p10_s8"
      },
      "text": "Depending on the C2 protocol used and the command being processed, control flow may take divergent paths through different functions only to converge again",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_57",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "rule",
        "sentence_id": "p4_r1"
      },
      "text": "I spent several hours on Russian language learning websites to study the pronunciation of Cyrillic characters and Russian words. Then, I looked up the top 600+ words and created a small dictionary. I added Russian language input to an analysis VM and used Microsoft’s on-screen keyboard (osk.exe) to navigate the Cyrillic keyboard layout and look up definitions.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "note": "rule or indicator snippet evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_58",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Fireeye_CARBANAK-Week-1-Rare-Occurrence(04-22-2019)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 10,
        "section": "rule",
        "sentence_id": "p10_r1"
      },
      "text": "the possibility of a local client to dispatch commands to CARBANAK without the use of a network. In fact, not only did we write such a client to aid in analysis and testing, but such a client, named botcmd.exe, was also present in the source dump.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.98,
      "note": "rule or indicator snippet evidence",
      "source": "document"
    }
